+- TARGET / EFFORT BOUNDARY: the action's offset is **0.0** and use_default_offset is **False**. Installed joint_actions.py first scales/clips the 50-Hz action and JointVelocityAction.apply_actions writes the held result into the joint velocity-target buffer. At each of the eight 400-Hz physics steps, articulation.py passes that target and current simulated joint velocity into IdealPDActuator.compute. It calculates **Kd*(target_velocity-measured_velocity)** with Kp zero and feedforward zero, clips using **effort_limit**, clears the outgoing position/velocity commands, and submits the resulting effort through the PhysX effort buffer/set_dof_actuation_forces. This is feedback torque control; the code does not overwrite actual joint speed with the target.
